.TH SHELLNAGA 1 "2026-11-16" "Shell'Naga 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shellnaga \- terminal and SSH client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shellnaga
[\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIID-or-NAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-new\-window\fR]
[\fIDIR\fR | \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B shellnaga run
.I PROGRAM
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B shellnaga mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shell'Naga is a fast terminal and SSH client with tabs, split panes, SFTP, serial, telnet, mosh,
tmux control mode and an encrypted password vault.
Started with no arguments it opens the window and restores the previous session.
If Shell'Naga is already running, a second launch hands its request to the running instance
and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fIID-or-NAME\fR
Start the first tab with this profile, given as a profile id (for example
.IR builtin:bash )
or as its name.
.TP
.BR \-\-cwd " " \fIDIR\fR
Start the first tab in this directory. A relative path is taken from the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window in addition to the session. With another instance running, only the new
window opens.
.TP
.BR \-\-after\-update
Used by the updater: the app was restarted after an update, and the session reopens.
.TP
.BR \-\-wait\-pid " " \fIN\fR
Wait for process \fIN\fR to end before taking over as the running instance.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version (\fBshellnaga\fR followed by the number) and exit with status 0. It opens no
window and needs no display.
.PP
A flag that is missing its value, and any argument not listed here, is ignored.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DIR
An existing local directory: the first tab starts there.
.TP
.I FILE
A script ending in
.BR .sh ,
.BR .bat ,
.B .cmd
or
.BR .ps1 :
opened in a tab that runs it.
.TP
.BR run " " \fIPROGRAM\fR " [" \fIARGS\fR ...]
Run the program in a tab that stays open after the program ends. Everything after
.B run
belongs to the program.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the stdio bridge of the local MCP server, so an AI assistant can talk to a running
Shell'Naga. It opens no window. The server is off by default and is turned on in Settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/shellnaga/
Settings, profiles and snippets.
